    content: `Blood groups are decided by two systems: ABO (A, B, AB or O) and the Rh factor (positive or negative). Together they give the eight familiar groups - A+, A-, B+, B-, AB+, AB-, O+ and O-.

The rules of compatibility are simple once you see the pattern. O-negative can be given to anyone, which is why it is called the universal donor and why blood banks are always short of it. AB-positive people can receive from anyone, but can only donate to other AB-positives.

In an emergency, doctors will not have time to look up your group - which is exactly why this platform gives every user an Emergency QR code. Anyone who scans it sees your blood group, allergies and emergency contact instantly, with no login.

Take a minute today to confirm your own blood group is correct on your Profile page, and tick the "willing to donate" box if you are. When someone in your city posts a request for your group, you could be the person who answers it.`,
